.TH "PB-CONFIG-REPOSITORY-CREDENTIALS" "1" "Sep 2026" "Paperboat" "Paperboat CLI"

.SH NAME
pb-config-repository-credentials - Store credentials privately on this machine


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpb config repository credentials [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Store credentials privately on this machine

.PP
Set or remove a private authentication profile for a custom Git repository on this machine. Profiles remain local to the machine and are configured independently from repository registration and the paths selected for synchronization.

.PP
Configuration commands distinguish local CLI settings from synchronized repository content. Inspect current state before changing it; synchronization reports conflicts instead of silently overwriting one side. The --json option provides structured output for scripts where supported.

.PP
With --json, this command group lists its available commands.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for credentials


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config\fP=""
	path to the CLI config file

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	print machine-readable JSON

.PP
\fB--no-customization\fP[=false]
	ignore local shortcuts, command defaults, and TUI preferences

.PP
\fB--server\fP=""
	paperboat-server base URL override

.PP
\fB--workspace\fP=""
	resource workspace selector: personal or a team slug


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBpb-config-repository(1)\fP, \fBpb-config-repository-credentials-remove(1)\fP, \fBpb-config-repository-credentials-set(1)\fP
